<Window x:Class="RxVerifyOverlay.Integrated.ControlBoxWindow"
        xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"
        xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
        Title="Rx Verify"
        WindowStyle="None"
        ResizeMode="NoResize"
        ShowInTaskbar="False"
        Topmost="True"
        WindowStartupLocation="Manual"
        Width="280" Height="36"
        Background="#FFF3F3F3"
        BorderBrush="#FFC8C8C8"
        BorderThickness="1"
        ShowActivated="False">
    <!--
        CONTROL BOX (item 2) — small interactive panel overlaid on
        PioneerRx (see IntegratedOverlayCoordinator's ControlBoxRightInsetDip/
        ControlBoxTopOffsetDip constants for exactly where — ROUND 4,
        branch fix/ribbon-topright-title, restored this to the top-right
        ribbon anchor ROUND 3 had briefly moved away from; see that
        round's own doc block, and ROUND 4's below, for why). UNLIKE
        IntegratedBoxesWindow, this is a NORMAL (non-click-through)
        window — it must receive clicks — so no WS_EX_TRANSPARENT/
        WS_EX_LAYERED here, just a light gray palette (see below) in a
        borderless, compact window that moves with PioneerRx every
        refresh tick (see RepositionPhysical in the code-behind).

        PALETTE (round 9, owner: "make the Integrated Display box be a
        lighter gray to blend in with Pioneer more, it's too harsh" —
        Pioneer's own ribbon area is a light, Windows-classic gray):
        replaced the original dark palette (matched MainWindow.xaml's
        #FF1E1E1E) with a light gray one so the box reads as PART OF
        Pioneer's chrome rather than a dark floating widget on top of
        it. MainWindow.xaml (the separate/full view) is intentionally
        untouched — this palette swap is scoped to the integrated
        control box only.

        LAYOUT (round 9, owner: "rearrange the display to make it user
        friendly and minimal"): collapsed from 3 rows to 2. ROUND 3
        (below) collapsed it further, to ONE row — see that doc block for
        the current shape; this paragraph is kept for history. Row 1
        reserves right margin for CloseButton's corner overlay (below) so
        the two never overlap.

        ROUND 3 (branch fix/overlay-compact-round3, Will verbatim, W-T86:
        "There is so much wasted space. We'll almost never change between
        the modes (OCR, etc), so that should go into a settings cog or
        something. Make this smaller and make it fit nicely in the gray
        area, don't cover any buttons or green."): collapsed from 2 rows
        to ONE slim row. Everything the pharmacist touches rarely now
        lives behind SettingsButton's cog flyout (SettingsPopup, below) —
        the Method (OCR/Escript) and Display (Integrated/Separate) toggle
        groups, the Hide (\) checkbox, the Mode (Verify/Order) dropdown,
        and "Full view"/"Copy (safe)". The always-visible row keeps only
        what changes or gets clicked every refresh: the status/timing
        text, Refresh, Feedback, the update dot (conditional), the cog
        itself, and CloseButton (corner overlay, unchanged). Width
        450 -> 230 (~49%, at the "half or less" target), Height 76 -> 36
        (one row instead of two). Nothing here removes functionality —
        every control that was clickable before still is, just one click
        further behind the cog instead of always on screen. This window
        is NOT currently draggable by the pharmacist (no DragMove/
        MouseDown handler exists) — its position is entirely computed
        every ~250ms tick by IntegratedOverlayCoordinator.UpdateControlBox,
        so "keep it draggable if it already is" (brief) is a no-op here.
        POSITION: this round ALSO moved the box's anchor from top-right
        to a reasoned bottom-left position (see the round's own commit) —
        ROUND 4 below reverts that specific part; the row/cog/size work
        above is otherwise untouched.

        ROUND 4 (branch fix/ribbon-topright-title, Will verbatim, after
        re-pulling round 3: "Much more compact which is good. But it
        needs to stay in the top right, not at the bottom left. And add
        the title of the app in there too RxVerify"): two tweaks, size
        unchanged from round 3 otherwise.
          1. ANCHOR reverted to top-right — see
             IntegratedOverlayCoordinator's ControlBoxRightInsetDip/
             ControlBoxTopOffsetDip (retuned for this box's new, smaller
             230-wide footprint; not just the old round-3-era numbers).
             Order mode's own top-right anchor (near Pioneer's "Color
             Legend") was never touched by round 3 OR this round.
          2. TITLE: a small bold "RxVerify" label added at the LEFT end
             of the row, before StatusTimeText (see below) — same
             FontSize as the other chrome text (9-10), just bold, so it
             reads as a label without competing with the status text or
             icons for attention. Width grew only by what the label
             needs: 230 -> 280 (+50).

        FEEDBACK + UPDATE REACHABILITY (branch fix/feedback-from-ribbon,
        Will verbatim: "I can't see anything on the overlay currently for
        feedback"): MainWindow.xaml's Feedback button and Update-ready
        banner are both invisible in Integrated mode — the pharmacist's
        DEFAULT mode, where this ribbon (not MainWindow) is the only
        surface up over PioneerRx. This window stays purely event-driven
        (see the class doc above) for both additions: FeedbackButton
        raises FeedbackRequested, UpdateDotButton raises UpdateRequested
        — MainWindow.xaml.cs (via IntegratedOverlayCoordinator, same
        relay pattern as every other *Requested event here) is what
        actually opens Integrated/FeedbackWindow or launches the update,
        reusing the exact same OpenFeedbackWindow/TriggerUpdate helpers
        its own Feedback button and Update banner call. UpdateDotButton
        is Collapsed by default and only takes up row-1 width when
        UpdateService.LastKnownUpdateAvailable is actually true (see
        code-behind SetUpdateAvailable) — Width grew 420 -> 450 (+30, the
        minimum needed) to fit the new always-present FeedbackButton
        icon without crowding StatusTimeText further; the dot itself
        costs nothing extra day-to-day.

        REVIEW FIX (focus-stealing): ShowActivated="False" plus
        WS_EX_NOACTIVATE (applied in code-behind's OnSourceInitialized)
        mean Show()/RepositionPhysical never steal keyboard focus/
        activation from PioneerRx — without this, refreshing the control
        box's position on every tick would yank focus away from whatever
        field the pharmacist is mid-typing into the instant Pioneer
        regains foreground. NOACTIVATE windows still receive mouse
        clicks normally, so the toggles/buttons keep working.
    -->
    <Window.Resources>
        <Style TargetType="Button">
            <Setter Property="Background" Value="#FFEBEBEB" />
            <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="#FF333333" />
            <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="#FFB5B5B5" />
            <Setter Property="BorderThickness" Value="1" />
            <Setter Property="Padding" Value="6,2" />
            <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="10" />
            <Setter Property="MinWidth" Value="20" />
            <Setter Property="MinHeight" Value="18" />
            <Setter Property="Cursor" Value="Hand" />
            <Style.Triggers>
                <Trigger Property="IsMouseOver" Value="True">
                    <Setter Property="Background" Value="#FFD9EBF9" />
                    <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="#FF99C9EF" />
                </Trigger>
                <Trigger Property="IsEnabled" Value="False">
                    <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="#FFAFAFAF" />
                    <Setter Property="Background" Value="#FFF7F7F7" />
                </Trigger>
            </Style.Triggers>
        </Style>
        <Style TargetType="RadioButton">
            <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="#FF333333" />
            <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="10" />
            <Setter Property="VerticalAlignment" Value="Center" />
            <Setter Property="VerticalContentAlignment" Value="Center" />
            <Setter Property="MinHeight" Value="16" />
            <Setter Property="Margin" Value="0,0,8,0" />
            <Style.Triggers>
                <Trigger Property="IsEnabled" Value="False">
                    <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="#FFAFAFAF" />
                </Trigger>
            </Style.Triggers>
        </Style>
        <Style TargetType="CheckBox">
            <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="#FF333333" />
            <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="9" />
            <Setter Property="VerticalAlignment" Value="Center" />
            <Setter Property="VerticalContentAlignment" Value="Center" />
            <Setter Property="MinHeight" Value="16" />
        </Style>
        <!-- Round 9: thin grouping border replacing "Source:"/"View:" text labels — visually groups the two toggle pairs without restating what their own Content already says. -->
        <Style x:Key="ToggleGroupBorderStyle" TargetType="Border">
            <Setter Property="Background" Value="#FFFCFCFC" />
            <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="#FFD5D5D5" />
            <Setter Property="BorderThickness" Value="1" />
            <Setter Property="CornerRadius" Value="3" />
            <Setter Property="Padding" Value="5,2" />
            <Setter Property="Margin" Value="0,0,6,0" />
        </Style>
        <!--
            MODE DROPDOWN (owner spec, 2026-08-14: "make the recommended
            order pops up in a window above the main Pioneer... make it
            say Mode: Order with a dropdown to switch back to verify"):
            replaces the old OrderAssistCheckBox. Two ComboBox instances
            share this style — ModeComboBoxNormal (in the full Verify-mode
            row below) and ModeComboBoxCompact (the ENTIRE content of
            CompactOrderPanel, shown only in Order mode) — see
            ControlBoxWindow.xaml.cs SetOrderAssistState for why there are
            two instances rather than one re-parented control.
        -->
        <Style x:Key="ModeComboBoxStyle" TargetType="ComboBox">
            <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="10" />
            <Setter Property="VerticalAlignment" Value="Center" />
            <Setter Property="MinHeight" Value="18" />
            <Setter Property="Padding" Value="4,1" />
        </Style>
    </Window.Resources>

    <Grid Margin="6">
        <!-- NORMAL content: status + a handful of icon actions, ONE slim row (round 3) -->
        <StackPanel x:Name="NormalPanel">
            <DockPanel Margin="0,0,20,0" LastChildFill="False">
                <!--
                    ROUND 4 (branch fix/ribbon-topright-title, Will
                    verbatim: "add the title of the app in there too
                    RxVerify") — the leftmost element in the row, docked
                    Left and declared FIRST so it sits before
                    StatusTimeText (also Dock=Left — DockPanel stacks
                    same-side children in declaration order). Bold to read
                    as a label distinct from the plain-weight status text
                    that follows it; same FontSize as the rest of this
                    row's chrome text.
                -->
                <TextBlock Text="RxVerify" DockPanel.Dock="Left" Foreground="#FF333333" FontSize="10" FontWeight="Bold" VerticalAlignment="Center" Margin="0,0,6,0" />
                <!--
                    Owner request (2026-08-13): "Remove the counter showing
                    the accurate/errors. that is not needed on the top
                    right box." Removed StatusSummaryText (the bold
                    "N✓ M✗" glyph counter, built by
                    IntegratedOverlayCoordinator.BuildStatusSummary — that
                    method and its call are gone too, see that file) along
                    with the StackPanel that only existed to hold it next
                    to StatusTimeText. StatusTimeText (the "Checked
                    h:mm:ss..." status/timing message — NOT a counter,
                    untouched by this request) now docks directly to the
                    left, with its stale left margin (it used to sit AFTER
                    the counter) removed so it isn't left with a dangling
                    gap.
                -->
                <TextBlock x:Name="StatusTimeText" Text="" DockPanel.Dock="Left" Foreground="#FF777777" FontSize="9" VerticalAlignment="Center" TextTrimming="CharacterEllipsis" />
                <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" DockPanel.Dock="Right">
                    <!-- Item 1: same Refresh action as the separate window's own Refresh button — icon-ish glyph, aligned/sized consistently with CloseButton's corner glyph below -->
                    <Button x:Name="RefreshButton" Content="&#8635;" FontSize="12" Padding="3,0" Margin="0,0,4,0" Click="OnRefreshClick" ToolTip="Refresh" />
                    <!--
                        Branch fix/feedback-from-ribbon: compact icon-only
                        Feedback affordance (envelope glyph, same
                        icon-button sizing as RefreshButton above) — this
                        ribbon is the only surface Will sees in Integrated
                        mode, so MainWindow's own Feedback button was
                        unreachable. Opens the exact same
                        Integrated/FeedbackWindow as MainWindow's button
                        (see FeedbackRequested in the code-behind and
                        MainWindow.xaml.cs's OpenFeedbackWindow helper).
                    -->
                    <Button x:Name="FeedbackButton" Content="&#9993;" FontSize="12" Padding="3,0" Margin="0,0,4,0" Click="OnFeedbackClick" ToolTip="Send feedback" />
                    <!--
                        Branch fix/feedback-from-ribbon: minimal update
                        indicator — a small dot, Collapsed by default (see
                        code-behind SetUpdateAvailable, driven by
                        UpdateService.LastKnownUpdateAvailable via
                        IntegratedOverlayCoordinator.SetUpdateAvailable)
                        so it costs zero row width until an update is
                        actually available. Click triggers the same
                        one-click bootstrap-and-exit update as
                        MainWindow's "Update ready" banner button (see
                        UpdateRequested / MainWindow.xaml.cs's
                        TriggerUpdate helper). Green fill matches the
                        banner's own accent color for the same signal.
                    -->
                    <Button x:Name="UpdateDotButton" Width="10" Height="10" Padding="0" Margin="0,0,6,0"
                            VerticalAlignment="Center" Click="OnUpdateDotClick" Cursor="Hand"
                            ToolTip="Update ready — click to update" Visibility="Collapsed">
                        <Button.Template>
                            <ControlTemplate TargetType="Button">
                                <Ellipse Fill="#FF2E7D32" Stroke="#FF1B3A1E" StrokeThickness="1" />
                            </ControlTemplate>
                        </Button.Template>
                    </Button>
                    <!--
                        ROUND 3 (branch fix/overlay-compact-round3): the
                        settings cog — Will verbatim, "We'll almost never
                        change between the modes (OCR, etc), so that
                        should go into a settings cog or something."
                        Toggles SettingsPopup (below) open/closed. Icon
                        button, same sizing as Refresh/Feedback above.
                    -->
                    <Button x:Name="SettingsButton" Content="&#9881;" FontSize="12" Padding="3,0" Click="OnSettingsClick" ToolTip="Settings (source, view, more)" />
                </StackPanel>
            </DockPanel>
        </StackPanel>

        <!--
            ROUND 3 SETTINGS FLYOUT (branch fix/overlay-compact-round3):
            everything the pharmacist rarely touches, moved off the
            always-visible row into this on-demand popup — see
            SettingsButton above and OnSettingsClick in the code-behind
            (a plain IsOpen toggle; no auto-dismiss-on-outside-click,
            deliberately: this window is WS_EX_NOACTIVATE and never takes
            focus during its own ~250ms reposition tick, and a
            StaysOpen="False" popup's dismiss behavior on a
            never-activated parent is untested territory this branch
            isn't the place to gamble on — a second cog click is a
            reliable, always-available close path instead). Square
            corners/opaque background on purpose (no AllowsTransparency)
            — same plain-rectangle aesthetic as the box itself, and one
            less interaction with the NOACTIVATE window style to worry
            about. ApplyModeLayout (below) force-closes this whenever
            Order mode toggles, so it can never be left open floating
            over a collapsed NormalPanel.

            Content is the OLD row-2 verbatim, MOVED here (not duplicated
            — each control has exactly one live instance, same as
            before): Method (Source) toggle group, Display (View) toggle
            group, the Hide (\) checkbox, the Mode (Verify/Order)
            dropdown, "Full view", and "Copy (safe)" — same x:Name's
            where code-behind reads one by name (the toggles/checkbox/
            combo), same Click/Checked/SelectionChanged handlers, same
            events out to IntegratedOverlayCoordinator. "Full view"/"Copy
            (safe)" never needed x:Name (their handlers read the Button
            from the Click event's own `sender`, not a named field — see
            OnOpenSeparateClick/OnCopyLogsNoHipaaClick), so they're
            unnamed here same as before.
        -->
        <Popup x:Name="SettingsPopup" PlacementTarget="{Binding ElementName=SettingsButton}" Placement="Bottom" StaysOpen="True">
            <Border Background="#FFF3F3F3" BorderBrush="#FFC8C8C8" BorderThickness="1" Padding="8">
                <StackPanel Width="240">
                    <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Margin="0,0,0,6">
                        <!-- Source (Method) toggle group -->
                        <Border Style="{StaticResource ToggleGroupBorderStyle}" ToolTip="Verification source">
                            <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal">
                                <RadioButton x:Name="MethodOcrRadioButton" GroupName="ControlBoxMethod" Content="OCR" Checked="OnMethodChanged" />
                                <RadioButton x:Name="MethodUiaRadioButton" GroupName="ControlBoxMethod" Content="Escript" Margin="0" Checked="OnMethodChanged" />
                            </StackPanel>
                        </Border>
                        <!-- Display mode (View) toggle group -->
                        <Border Style="{StaticResource ToggleGroupBorderStyle}" ToolTip="Display mode">
                            <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal">
                                <RadioButton x:Name="DisplayIntegratedRadioButton" GroupName="ControlBoxDisplay" Content="Integrated" Checked="OnDisplayModeChanged" />
                                <RadioButton x:Name="DisplaySeparateRadioButton" GroupName="ControlBoxDisplay" Content="Separate" Margin="0" Checked="OnDisplayModeChanged" />
                            </StackPanel>
                        </Border>
                    </StackPanel>
                    <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Margin="0,0,0,6">
                        <!--
                            Item 2: hides the verdict BOXES layer only (this
                            control box stays up) — kept in sync with the global
                            `\` hotkey (see code-behind's RegisterHotKey/WndProc);
                            session-only, always starts unchecked on app restart
                            (never persisted to settings.json) so a pharmacist can
                            never inherit a hidden overlay from a previous shift.
                        -->
                        <CheckBox x:Name="HideOverlayCheckBox" Content="Hide (\)" VerticalAlignment="Center" Margin="0,0,8,0" Checked="OnHideOverlayToggled" Unchecked="OnHideOverlayToggled" ToolTip="Hide overlay (\)" />
                        <!--
                            MODE DROPDOWN (owner spec, 2026-08-14) — REPLACES the
                            old "Order Assist" checkbox. Two items only:
                            "Mode: Verify" (index 0, the default — OverlaySettings.
                            OrderAssistEnabled defaults false) and "Mode: Order"
                            (index 1). Selecting "Mode: Order" here is what
                            triggers ControlBoxWindow.xaml.cs SetOrderAssistState
                            to swap NormalPanel out for CompactOrderPanel below
                            (see that method's doc) — this whole flyout closes
                            with it (ApplyModeLayout), since the whole point is
                            the box no longer blocks Pioneer's popup once Order
                            mode is active.
                        -->
                        <ComboBox x:Name="ModeComboBoxNormal" Style="{StaticResource ModeComboBoxStyle}" Width="110" SelectionChanged="OnModeComboBoxChanged" ToolTip="Order mode highlights zero order quantities and cheaper secondary substitutions on Pioneer's order screens; Verify mode resumes normal rx-verification highlights">
                            <ComboBoxItem Content="Mode: Verify" />
                            <ComboBoxItem Content="Mode: Order" />
                        </ComboBox>
                    </StackPanel>
                    <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal">
                        <Button Content="Full view" Margin="0,0,4,0" Click="OnOpenSeparateClick" ToolTip="Open full view" />
                        <Button Content="Copy (safe)" Click="OnCopyLogsNoHipaaClick" ToolTip="Copy logs (no HIPAA)" />
                    </StackPanel>
                </StackPanel>
            </Border>
        </Popup>

        <!--
            COMPACT ORDER-MODE PANEL (owner spec, 2026-08-14: "should
            change the layout of the box to make it fit where it's not
            blocking anything, like just next to the 'Color legend' on
            the top right, and just make it say Mode: Order with a
            dropdown to switch back to verify"): the ENTIRE control box
            content while Order mode is active — NormalPanel above is
            hidden outright (see SetOrderAssistState), and
            IntegratedOverlayCoordinator repositions/resizes the whole
            window to its small ORDER-MODE constants whenever this is
            showing (see that class's OrderModeControlBox*Dip docs).
            Collapsed by default (Verify mode, the default state).

            REVIEW FIX (pre-merge, 2026-08-14 — escape-hatch hardening):
            ModeComboBoxCompact is the FIRST ComboBox ever placed on this
            WS_EX_NOACTIVATE window — plain Buttons (RefreshButton,
            CloseButton, etc.) are proven to work here, but a ComboBox's
            dropdown POPUP is a separate, unproven top-level window of its
            own on a non-activating parent. If that popup ever failed to
            open on a real workstation, the pharmacist would be stuck in
            Order mode with no way out (CloseButton is hidden in this
            panel — see SetOrderAssistState). VerifyEscapeButton is a
            tiny, quiet, PLAIN Button (the one control type already
            proven reliable here) that goes straight back to Verify mode
            — same code path as picking "Mode: Verify" in the dropdown,
            see OnVerifyEscapeButtonClick — regardless of whether the
            ComboBox popup itself works.
        -->
        <StackPanel x:Name="CompactOrderPanel" Visibility="Collapsed" Orientation="Horizontal" HorizontalAlignment="Center" VerticalAlignment="Center">
            <ComboBox x:Name="ModeComboBoxCompact" Style="{StaticResource ModeComboBoxStyle}" Width="120" SelectionChanged="OnModeComboBoxChanged" ToolTip="Switch back to Verify mode to resume rx-verification highlights">
                <ComboBoxItem Content="Mode: Verify" />
                <ComboBoxItem Content="Mode: Order" />
            </ComboBox>
            <Button x:Name="VerifyEscapeButton" Content="Verify" Margin="4,0,0,0" Padding="4,1" FontSize="9" MinHeight="18" MinWidth="0" Click="OnVerifyEscapeButtonClick" ToolTip="Switch straight back to Verify mode" />
        </StackPanel>

        <!--
            MAXIMIZED-ONLY guard (item 3) — shown ON TOP of NormalPanel
            (not instead of it) whenever PioneerRx is attached but not
            maximized; SetMaximizedGuardState also greys every toggle
            except DisplaySeparateRadioButton, so the pharmacist can
            always escape back to Separate without maximizing first.
        -->
        <Border x:Name="MaximizeNoteBorder" Background="#FFFFF4CE" BorderBrush="#FFFFD666" BorderThickness="1" CornerRadius="3" Padding="6,3" VerticalAlignment="Top" HorizontalAlignment="Stretch" Visibility="Collapsed">
            <TextBlock Text="Maximize PioneerRx to use integrated view" Foreground="#FF7A5900" FontSize="10" FontWeight="Bold" TextWrapping="Wrap" />
        </Border>

        <!--
            Item 8: terminates the whole app (Application.Current.Shutdown(),
            via MainWindow's own existing Close()/Closed cleanup path — see
            code-behind). Round-1 review flagged this as the missing
            affordance: without it, integrated mode had no way to quit
            without first opening the full separate view. Deliberately
            plain/quiet (no red hover, no border, transparent at rest) —
            this is a corner escape hatch, not an action button, and must
            never draw the eye the way Refresh/Copy logs/toggles do.
        -->
        <Button x:Name="CloseButton" Content="&#10005;" Click="OnCloseClick"
                Width="18" Height="18" Padding="0" FontSize="9"
                HorizontalAlignment="Right" VerticalAlignment="Top" Margin="0,-6,-6,0"
                Foreground="#FF888888" Background="Transparent" BorderThickness="0"
                ToolTip="Close Rx Verify">
            <Button.Style>
                <Style TargetType="Button">
                    <Setter Property="Cursor" Value="Hand" />
                    <Style.Triggers>
                        <Trigger Property="IsMouseOver" Value="True">
                            <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="#FF333333" />
                            <Setter Property="Background" Value="#FFF3D6D6" />
                        </Trigger>
                    </Style.Triggers>
                </Style>
            </Button.Style>
        </Button>
    </Grid>
</Window>
